5. F-1 FIX ADDENDUM (impl-review iteration 1, BLOCKING finding F-1)
======================================================================
Finding: run.sh's pre-existing ACTION=close branch (skills/earn/run.sh:214-222) still read the
`closed_pnl_usd` field REQ-A1 removes from hl.py's JSON output. Since `.get('closed_pnl_usd', 0)`
silently defaults to 0 with no exception, every explicit HL close was recording a fabricated
$0.00 ledger line — the exact bug class this feature exists to kill, moved from hl.py into
run.sh, unguarded by any REQ/PROP/test in the original verification architecture.

Spec fix (fresh option (a) from the finding): REQ-A3 added to behavioral-spec.md Group A — the
reconciler (hl.py reconcile) is the SOLE recorder of HL realized P&L; run.sh's ACTION=close
branch must not read the removed field and must not append any earn_usdc/cost_usdc ledger line
of its own for the close. EDGE-12 added documenting the one-wake-later recording path (reconcile
sees nothing new the wake of the close itself; the next wake's reconcile picks up the now-settled
fill). PROP-024 added to verification-architecture.md (Tier 0, required) — static: 0 matches for
`closed_pnl_usd` anywhere in run.sh (code or comments); structural: no `record_line` call inside
the ACTION=close execution branch specifically (disambiguated from the earlier anti-churn
cooldown guard's compound condition, which also contains the substring `ACTION" = "close"`).
Obligation count updated 29->30 total, 27->28 Tier-0.

